                "The toolkit is organized around a tiered pledge model that meets faculty where they are, rather than requiring an all-or-nothing commitment that many educators feel unprepared to make.\n\n"
                "WHAT'S INCLUDED\n\n"
                "The Three-Tier Pledge System:\n\n"
                "Tier 1 — Awareness: The educator commits to learning the basics. They read the Trans Student Support Resource Guide, complete a one-hour self-paced professional development module, and agree to use correct names and pronouns for their students. This is the entry point — a meaningful but accessible commitment that any educator can make.\n\n"
                "Tier 2 — Active Support: The educator commits to being a go-to resource. They display an Ally Pledge commitment card in their classroom, complete the full 90-minute Allyship Training, commit to responding when they witness trans-directed harassment or microaggressions, and agree to keep a copy of the Trans Student Support Resource Guide accessible for student reference.\n\n"
                "Tier 3 — Advocacy: The educator commits to institutional change. In addition to Tier 1 and 2 commitments, they actively participate in policy discussions, serve as a faculty sponsor for the GSA or trans advocacy initiatives, advocate within their department for inclusive curriculum, and attend at least one professional development event per year related to trans-inclusive education.\n\n"
